# opensuse -- openSUSE Tumbleweed, and what says ID_LIKE=opensuse (Leap,
# Slowroll: by family, not proven); os-release's own ID there is
# opensuse-tumbleweed, so the family is the ID_LIKE word. The same six
# keys as debian.env (contract 3). zypper is asked with -y; a name counts
# as installed when any installed package provides it (rpm -q
# --whatprovides: python3 is python313's capability, no package of its
# own). A rolling distro: the full upgrade is `sudo zypper dup`, never
# `zypper up`, and an install zypper refuses is a todo naming it. Every
# name here is credited in CREDITS.md.
PM=zypper
PM_INSTALL=sudo zypper install -y
PM_TARGET=openSUSE Tumbleweed
# core -- the AI (+ PKG_AI for vulkan); tar unpacks the engine, and a
# minimal Tumbleweed install has none
PKG_CORE=git curl ca-certificates python3 tar
# llama.cpp's build needs OpenMP: libgomp1, Debian's name for it too
PKG_ENGINE=libgomp1
# the vulkan build only: the loader and Mesa's two drivers
PKG_AI=libvulkan1 libvulkan_radeon libvulkan_intel
